  "conclusion": "Kernels + gaps account for the decode wall exactly at both depths. The depth growth is inter-kernel dispatch gap time: ~1,740-1,815 launches per step each incur 2.7 us (p512) to 6.2 us (p4096) of GPU-side queue latency. Host-side Python cost removal cannot reduce it (the build-identity A/B tie proved that). The lever is fewer, larger launches: extend the existing per-layer MoE HIP graph to the whole decode step, or fuse launch chains."
